# Workflow configuration. Saved by the orchestrator web UI, which does not keep comments.
#
# The seeded workflows are the exercises of the Software Factory course, one per session
# (ex01 to ex09). Their agents and policies are the group `course` in services/registry/seed.
#
# Each step runs on the Temporal task queue named by `service`. Steps without
# depends_on receive the run input; other steps receive the outputs of their
# dependencies as an ordered list of items. These services are special:
#   agent  runs the pinned agent named by `agent` (for example course/intake@v1)
#   gate   waits until a person approves or rejects in the factory UI
#   route  starts the workflow named in the `route` field of its input artifact
#   interactive  holds the step while a person works with its agents in a chat session
#   workflow     runs the workflow version named by `workflow` (for example build@v1) as
#                a child run; its output is the output of that workflow's single final step
#   team   a lead agent (`agent`) and other members (`agents`, `workflows`) exchange messages
#          over `channels` until the lead finishes the team; a gate with `on_reject` sends a
#          rejection and its reason back to the named team step and reopens afterwards
#   merge  waits until every step in `depends_on` has delivered and forwards their results
#          together; `capacity` (default 16) limits the waiting entries, and the run fails when
#          an entry stays incomplete for `input_timeout` seconds (default 300)
#   batch  collects results from the steps in `depends_on` and forwards them together once it
#          holds `size` items, or fewer once `input_timeout` seconds (default 300) have passed
#          since the last one
# The steps after a merge or batch run once per forwarded message; pass n of a step stores
# its artifact as runs/<trace>/<step>.pass-<n>.
# Steps of a routed workflow store their artifacts under runs/<trace>/<route step>/.
#
# The file keeps every version of every workflow: saving a workflow adds an entry with the
# next `version`. An entry without a version is v1. Workflow references pin a version
# (name@vN); a reference without one is pinned to the newest version when the file is loaded.
workflows:
  - name: ex01-team-standing
    description: "Session 1 exercise, Where Does Your Team Stand: fill in the worksheet in a chat and get a summary of the chosen practice."
    steps:
      - id: worksheet
        service: interactive
        agent: course/standing-coach@v1
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: summary
        service: agent
        agent: course/standing-summary@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - worksheet
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
  - name: ex02-research-workflow
    description: "Session 2 exercise, Build a Research Workflow: plan a research question, research two sub-questions in parallel, and write one report for a person to accept."
    steps:
      - id: plan
        service: agent
        agent: course/research-planner@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 98
      - id: research-a
        service: agent
        agent: course/researcher@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - plan
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
      - id: research-b
        service: agent
        agent: course/researcher@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - plan
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 166
      - id: collect
        service: merge
        depends_on:
          - research-a
          - research-b
        input_timeout: 1800
        position:
          x: 796
          y: 98
      - id: report
        service: agent
        agent: course/research-writer@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - collect
        position:
          x: 1064
          y: 98
      - id: decide
        service: gate
        question: Is the research report good enough to use? A rejection needs a reason.
        depends_on:
          - report
        position:
          x: 1332
          y: 98
  - name: ex03-system-design
    description: "Session 3 exercise, System Design for Your Own Software Factory: design the services with their requirements and approvals, and check the design."
    steps:
      - id: design
        service: agent
        agent: course/factory-architect@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: check
        service: agent
        agent: course/design-checker@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - design
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
      - id: decide
        service: gate
        question: Does the checked design describe the factory you want to build?
        depends_on:
          - check
        position:
          x: 796
          y: 30
  - name: ex04-intake-triage
    description: "Session 4 exercise, Intake and Triage: run the intake checks on a signal, triage the work item by the routing rules, and confirm the triage."
    steps:
      - id: intake
        service: agent
        agent: course/intake@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: triage
        service: agent
        agent: course/triage@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - intake
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
      - id: confirm
        service: gate
        question: Is the triage correct, and may the work item go to the proposed next owner?
        depends_on:
          - triage
        position:
          x: 796
          y: 30
  - name: ex05-architecture-review
    description: "Session 5 exercise, An Architecture Review Agent: review a spec against the current ADRs and the spec policy, and decide on the findings."
    steps:
      - id: review
        service: agent
        agent: course/architecture-reviewer@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: decide
        service: gate
        question: Do you accept the reviewer's findings and their decisions for this spec?
        depends_on:
          - review
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
  - name: ex06-implementation
    description: "Session 6 exercise, Compose and Run an Implementation Agent: build one requirement from a spec and a plan, and check what the run hands over."
    steps:
      - id: build
        service: agent
        agent: course/feature-builder@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: check
        service: agent
        agent: course/delivery-checker@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - build
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
      - id: decide
        service: gate
        question: Do you take over this delivery to run its checks yourself?
        depends_on:
          - check
        position:
          x: 796
          y: 30
  - name: ex07-guardrails
    description: "Session 7 exercise, Guardrails for CL-7: write the guardrails for a rule, try to get around them, and decide whether they hold."
    steps:
      - id: author
        service: agent
        agent: course/guardrail-author@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: attack
        service: agent
        agent: course/guardrail-attacker@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - author
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
      - id: decide
        service: gate
        question: Do the guardrails stop every attempt well enough to use them?
        depends_on:
          - attack
        position:
          x: 796
          y: 30
  - name: ex08-pr-review
    description: "Session 8 exercise, Verify and Review a Pull Request: a spec agent and a QA agent check a pull request, and a dossier prepares the decision."
    steps:
      - id: spec-review
        service: agent
        agent: course/spec-agent@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: qa-review
        service: agent
        agent: course/qa-agent@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 166
      - id: collect
        service: merge
        depends_on:
          - spec-review
          - qa-review
        input_timeout: 1800
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 98
      - id: dossier
        service: agent
        agent: course/dossier-writer@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - collect
        position:
          x: 796
          y: 98
      - id: decide
        service: gate
        question: Do you follow the route the dossier proposes for this pull request?
        depends_on:
          - dossier
        position:
          x: 1064
          y: 98
  - name: ex09-trust-runs
    description: "Session 9 exercise, Would You Trust These Agent Runs: label agent runs from their records and propose one check for a failure found."
    steps:
      - id: label
        service: agent
        agent: course/run-reviewer@v1
        timeout: 10m
        position:
          x: 260
          y: 30
      - id: check
        service: agent
        agent: course/check-author@v1
        timeout: 10m
        depends_on:
          - label
        position:
          x: 528
          y: 30
      - id: decide
        service: gate
        question: Would you add the proposed check to the factory?
        depends_on:
          - check
        position:
          x: 796
          y: 30
